1
00:00:01,520 --> 00:00:03,650
Wealth, fame, power...

2
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:07,820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,
obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:07,820 --> 00:00:11,660
What he said in his final moments
drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:11,660 --> 00:00:13,660
You want my treasure?

5
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:15,450
Go ahead.

6
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:16,660
Find it!

7
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,250
Everything is right where I left it!

8
00:00:21,670 --> 00:00:26,380
People set their sights on the Grand Line
in pursuit of their dreams.

9
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,630
The world has truly entered
the Great Pirate Era!

10
00:01:50,050 --> 00:01:54,720
Townsfolks' Emergency Shelter

11
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:54,430
This is strange...

12
00:01:54,430 --> 00:01:57,640
The mayor's usually not
gone for so long.

13
00:01:57,640 --> 00:02:00,200
Something must have
happened in town!

14
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:03,640
Also, there's been
more cannon fire than usual!

15
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,860
All right! I'll go into town
and check it out!

16
00:02:05,860 --> 00:02:07,270
You all stay here!

17
00:02:07,270 --> 00:02:08,520
I'm coming too!

18
00:02:08,520 --> 00:02:13,500
Don't be an idiot! Those wretched
Buggy Pirates are in town!

19
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:15,920
And that's precisely
why I'm coming too!

20
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:20,350
What kind of citizens are we
if we can't even keep our mayor safe?!

21
00:02:20,350 --> 00:02:24,790
It's no use trying to stop us!
This is all of our own accord!

22
00:02:26,040 --> 00:02:27,490
Fine. Do what you want.

23
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:28,920
Let's go, everyone!

24
00:02:35,340 --> 00:02:40,670
Pirate Buggy "the Clown"

25
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:40,260
Never in my life has anyone
made me angrier than he did!

26
00:02:40,260 --> 00:02:44,660
That bastard Shanks stole
enormous riches from me!

27
00:02:44,660 --> 00:02:47,260
I don't know how you two
are connected,

28
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:50,190
but I'll say whatever
I want about him!

29
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,640
– Get him! Get him! Fight!
– Stand your ground, you two!

30
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,490
The North Pole!

31
00:02:57,490 --> 00:02:58,760
No, the South Pole!

32
00:02:58,760 --> 00:02:59,920
You won't budge, huh?!

33
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:02,370
You got it! And I'll keep
sayin' it cause I'm right!

34
00:03:02,370 --> 00:03:05,860
Oh, you got guts! I'm gonna
settle this once and for all today!

35
00:03:05,860 --> 00:03:07,200
Go ahead and try it!

36
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:10,350
Alright, you bastard!
I'm gonna bust you up flashily!

37
00:03:10,350 --> 00:03:11,150
You wish!

38
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:12,320
Knock that off!

39
00:03:13,190 --> 00:03:16,050
Who cares whether it's colder
at the South or North Pole?!

40
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:19,880
If you wanna know that badly,
go to both and find out!

41
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:20,800
Now cool it!

42
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,970
A ship!

43
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:25,780
Enemy ship to the north-northeast!

44
00:03:25,780 --> 00:03:28,520
Alright, get ready! Time to fight!

45
00:03:29,660 --> 00:03:32,240
Great! I'm gonna plunder up a storm!

46
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,520
You look happy, Buggy!

47
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:37,680
Obviously! Enemy ships
are like treasure chests.

48
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,390
Pirates love to crack 'em open!

49
00:03:39,390 --> 00:03:40,840
Am I wrong?!

50
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:42,910
Well, there is some truth to that.

51
00:03:42,910 --> 00:03:44,120
You're too soft!

52
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:48,740
You and everyone else here
never talk seriously about treasure!

53
00:03:48,750 --> 00:03:51,290
You don't know what
it means to be a pirate!

54
00:03:59,060 --> 00:04:01,010
Wh-What's this?!

55
00:04:01,010 --> 00:04:03,680
A-A-A treasure map!

56
00:04:04,290 --> 00:04:07,640
I've never seen one before! Awesome!

57
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:11,330
It's just sitting there
on the bottom of the ocean?

58
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:20,870
Yes! Now my life is flashily decided!

59
00:04:27,720 --> 00:04:30,360
Today was another easy win!

60
00:04:30,360 --> 00:04:31,860
Hey! Drink up!

61
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:33,240
Hey, Buggy!

62
00:04:33,240 --> 00:04:37,120
You're not gonna party with us?
The loot today was really something!

63
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:40,820
I-I ain't got nothin',
and I don't know nothin'!

64
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:42,660
What are you talking about?

65
00:04:42,660 --> 00:04:44,260
Oh, uh...

66
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:51,680
You said you were gonna
leave this ship someday.

67
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,630
Got any big plans?

68
00:04:53,630 --> 00:04:55,490
I'm gonna have my own ship.

69
00:04:55,490 --> 00:04:59,110
I'll gather a reliable crew
and then see the world.

70
00:04:59,110 --> 00:05:03,600
It'll be at a nice, leisurely pace,
and as a pirate, of course.

71
00:05:03,600 --> 00:05:07,050
You always spout that sentimental crap.

72
00:05:06,100 --> 00:05:07,050
Say what?!

73
00:05:07,050 --> 00:05:10,060
I can't deny you're good in a fight,

74
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:14,200
but if you were a bit more ruthless,
I may have let you be one of my henchmen.

75
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,620
Me? One of your
henchmen? Get real!

76
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:17,200
Huh?

77
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:20,210
Our outlooks are too different,

78
00:05:20,210 --> 00:05:22,860
so we should just go
our separate ways.

79
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:24,040
That's what pirates do.

80
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:27,320
Who made you
the expert on pirates, huh?

81
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:31,170
And if we ever cross prows,
we'll also need to cross swords.

82
00:05:31,170 --> 00:05:33,980
Yeah. That's another thing pirates do.

83
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:36,270
You never make sense.

84
00:05:37,140 --> 00:05:40,900
Anyway, you said
something about loot...

85
00:05:40,900 --> 00:05:42,940
Yeah, we found a devil fruit.

86
00:05:42,940 --> 00:05:43,990
Devil fruit?

87
00:05:43,990 --> 00:05:47,540
I heard they're
incarnations of sea devils.

88
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:50,070
They say if you eat one
you gain a devil's powers,

89
00:05:50,070 --> 00:05:53,540
but the sea will hate you
and make you sink like an anchor.

90
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:56,710
You'd have to be stupid
to eat something like that!

91
00:05:56,710 --> 00:06:01,700
I'd never get all that treasure
on the ocean floor if I couldn't swim!

92
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:06,810
Still, I bet it'd sell
for 100 million belly...

93
00:06:08,620 --> 00:06:09,710
What?!

94
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:15,060
I, pirate apprentice Buggy,
will now eat this devil fruit!

95
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:19,480
Kids are a riot a minute,
never thinking of the consequences.

96
00:06:21,400 --> 00:06:22,610
He ate it!

97
00:06:24,680 --> 00:06:27,740
Well, Buggy? Anything different
about your body?

98
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,740
No... Not really...

99
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:31,320
So, what? Was it fake?

100
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:36,150
Not surprising. I've only heard
about devil fruits from rumors.

101
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:41,260
Yes! That worked flashily well!

102
00:06:41,260 --> 00:06:44,000
What I ate this afternoon
was a fake I made!

103
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,730
Can't believe everything
went so smoothly!

104
00:06:46,730 --> 00:06:49,770
Now to jump ship
before they find out the truth!

105
00:06:49,770 --> 00:06:52,800
The money from the devil fruit?
The map's treasure?

106
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:56,080
That will get me
a pirate crew right away!

107
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,500
Hey, Buggy!

108
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,320
Whatcha grinning about?

109
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:01,780
Oh, it's you!
Don't scare me like that!

110
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:03,810
What kind of face is that?

111
00:07:03,810 --> 00:07:07,780
If you steal too much from the kitchen,
the cook will give you hell!

112
00:07:07,780 --> 00:07:10,000
Whew, that was close...

113
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:12,870
Oh, that reminds me!
The captain just–

114
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:21,480
– What the...?!
– Shanks! Damn you!

115
00:07:21,480 --> 00:07:23,780
My... My... I'm...

116
00:07:24,460 --> 00:07:26,080
What's that scrap of paper?

117
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:28,750
Ahh! My map!

118
00:07:28,750 --> 00:07:30,550
H-Hey, Buggy!

119
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:35,810
Wh-What gives? I can't move...

120
00:07:35,810 --> 00:07:40,770
So then it's true that you
sink like an anchor?! Crap!

121
00:07:40,770 --> 00:07:42,980
Hey! Buggy! What are you doing?

122
00:07:42,980 --> 00:07:44,870
You're great at swimming!

123
00:07:47,820 --> 00:07:48,890
Buggy!

124
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:52,860
H-Help me...

125
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:56,570
I'll save you, Buggy!

126
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:08,040
So Shanks saved you?

127
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:10,130
That's not what I'm trying to say!

128
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:15,300
Because of him, my plan in life
was suddenly delayed ten years!

129
00:08:15,300 --> 00:08:17,140
And then I had a revelation!

130
00:08:17,140 --> 00:08:21,270
If below the sea is off limits,
I'll obtain all the treasure above land...

131
00:08:21,780 --> 00:08:25,020
using this Part-Part power.

132
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:32,650
That's why I won't let anyone
who touches my treasure live!

133
00:08:34,570 --> 00:08:36,730
Let go...

134
00:08:36,730 --> 00:08:39,180
of my treasure!

135
00:08:39,180 --> 00:08:40,870
Crap! He spotted me!

136
00:08:42,790 --> 00:08:45,750
Don't think you can
escape me, Nami!

137
00:08:45,750 --> 00:08:48,750
I'm going to flashily
slice you to pieces!

138
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:06,600
M-My parts... my special parts!

139
00:09:07,020 --> 00:09:09,570
You're still dealing with me!

140
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,440
Hey!

141
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:16,420
Leave that treasure
and get out of here!

142
00:09:16,420 --> 00:09:17,620
He'll just keep coming.

143
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:18,410
No!

144
00:09:18,410 --> 00:09:21,760
Leave the treasure and
get out of here?! Absolutely not!

145
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:24,540
Why should I 
leave my treasure behind?!

146
00:09:25,220 --> 00:09:27,540
Your treasure?!

147
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:29,020
Of course it is!

148
00:09:29,020 --> 00:09:31,240
I'm a thief who only
steals from pirates,

149
00:09:31,240 --> 00:09:33,520
and I just stole from a pirate!

150
00:09:34,230 --> 00:09:38,100
Meaning, this treasure
now belongs to me!

151
00:09:38,100 --> 00:09:40,500
Ah, I see!

152
00:09:40,500 --> 00:09:43,600
My ass, it is! That's my treasure!

153
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,400
Do you think stealing it
makes it yours?!

154
00:09:47,400 --> 00:09:50,610
Honestly! What kind of
upbringing did you have?!

155
00:09:50,610 --> 00:09:54,810
A criminal, trying to lecture
another criminal? That's rich!

156
00:09:54,840 --> 00:09:55,770
What?!

157
00:09:55,780 --> 00:10:01,200
I haven't fallen so low that I need
to be lectured by pirates!

158
00:10:04,100 --> 00:10:07,160
I hope you're ready to face
the consequences, Nami...

159
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:11,040
Part-Part...

160
00:10:12,040 --> 00:10:15,510
Festival!

161
00:10:17,980 --> 00:10:21,880
Just try and help your friend
if you can, Gum-Gum!

162
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:26,180
Damn, he's split apart even more!

163
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,270
What's this?

164
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,460
Nami!

165
00:10:30,190 --> 00:10:32,980
Give me my back my treasure!

166
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:32,980
You wish!

167
00:10:35,690 --> 00:10:37,680
Coochie, coochie, coo!

168
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:45,070
Damn, you're stubborn!

169
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:49,060
Knock it off!

170
00:10:49,060 --> 00:10:52,410
No, you knock it off!

171
00:10:57,610 --> 00:11:00,680
Thanks for returning the treasure!

172
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:07,220
Let go?! This is my treasure!

173
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:07,220
Let go! Let go! That's mine!

174
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:08,760
You let go!

175
00:11:11,770 --> 00:11:14,570
Die!

176
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,310
I told you, you're dealing with me!

177
00:11:45,180 --> 00:11:48,390
That last kick
was for the old mayor guy!

178
00:11:50,340 --> 00:11:53,180
Th-Thanks, I owe you one.

179
00:11:53,180 --> 00:11:54,830
Yeah, no problem!

180
00:11:57,000 --> 00:11:59,270
Oh yeah! The map!

181
00:11:58,030 --> 00:11:59,270
My treasure–

182
00:11:59,270 --> 00:12:03,240
This isn't over yet, Gum-Gum!

183
00:12:03,240 --> 00:12:04,360
He's still alive!

184
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,840
Shut up!

185
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:09,200
How dare you flashily do this to me!

186
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,520
You'll pay for this!

187
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,990
Assemble! Part-Part parts!

188
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:26,460
Huh?

189
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:30,320
Looking for these?!

190
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:32,590
My parts!

191
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,270
Way to go, thief!

192
00:12:36,270 --> 00:12:37,940
D-D-Don't!

193
00:12:37,940 --> 00:12:39,670
Beat it, Buggy!

194
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:41,900
Gum-Gum...

195
00:12:43,040 --> 00:12:46,190
Bazooka!

196
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:58,270
I win!

197
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:03,600
Hey! Captain Buggy went flying!

198
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:06,900
Wh-What do we do?!

199
00:13:06,900 --> 00:13:08,680
Play dead for now!

200
00:13:08,700 --> 00:13:09,470
Good idea!

201
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:16,700
It's all torn up now...

202
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:18,260
Well, that's okay!

203
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:19,640
I can still put it on,

204
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,270
plus I sent Buggy flying,
so I'm satisfied.

205
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:30,680
It's all right. I'll fix it for you later.

206
00:13:30,680 --> 00:13:31,950
Huh? What?

207
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,350
Nothing!

208
00:13:33,350 --> 00:13:36,780
So anyway, I split it into two bags,
so carry half of it!

209
00:13:36,780 --> 00:13:38,960
It's too heavy for me!

210
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:40,850
There sure is a lot!

211
00:13:40,850 --> 00:13:45,160
If nothing else, Buggy does know
quality treasure when he sees it!

212
00:13:45,160 --> 00:13:47,880
All this should go for no less
than ten million belly!

213
00:13:53,020 --> 00:13:54,560
Here you go.

214
00:13:54,580 --> 00:13:55,200
Huh?

215
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:58,400
It's a map to the Grand Line.
You want it, right?

216
00:13:58,400 --> 00:13:59,440
You're giving it up?!

217
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,090
You did save me.

218
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:03,340
Thanks, Nami!

219
00:14:03,340 --> 00:14:06,460
I finally got a map to the Grand Line!

220
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:08,020
Hooray!

221
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:11,720
Oh! Does that mean
you'll join our crew now?!

222
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:14,790
I told you I'm never
going to join a pirate crew!

223
00:14:15,740 --> 00:14:19,890
But okay! Staying with you guys
seems profitable enough.

224
00:14:19,890 --> 00:14:22,590
But let me be clear:
We're just teaming up.

225
00:14:22,590 --> 00:14:24,160
Don't forget that!

226
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:25,880
Yeah!

227
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:31,420
Hey! Zoro! Wake up! Zoro!

228
00:14:31,420 --> 00:14:32,810
We're going!

229
00:14:33,810 --> 00:14:35,640
Did we take care of everything?

230
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:39,310
Yeah! We also got the map
and a navigator!

231
00:14:43,760 --> 00:14:47,380
No good... Out of blood...
I don't think I can walk.

232
00:14:47,380 --> 00:14:51,440
Ya think?! If either of you could walk
after that, you wouldn't be human!

233
00:14:51,440 --> 00:14:53,240
Wait, why me too?

234
00:14:53,240 --> 00:14:55,660
You're the most suspicious of all!

235
00:14:55,660 --> 00:14:57,860
Anyway, let's help the mayor.

236
00:14:57,860 --> 00:14:59,250
Oh, yeah!

237
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:02,240
We gotta wake up
the old mayor guy now.

238
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,210
You, there!

239
00:15:03,210 --> 00:15:05,240
Are you outsiders?!

240
00:15:05,240 --> 00:15:07,360
Yeah. Who are you?

241
00:15:07,340 --> 00:15:10,180
We're this town's citizens!

242
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:12,240
Did the pirates disband or something?

243
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,380
If you know anything, tell us!

244
00:15:15,380 --> 00:15:18,060
Oh, it's just the citizens!

245
00:15:18,060 --> 00:15:19,920
I was scared it was more pirates.

246
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:21,100
Oh, Mayor!

247
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,830
Oh, no! Say something!

248
00:15:22,830 --> 00:15:24,040
Hey! Mayor!

249
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:26,220
– He's out cold!
– This had to be the pirates!

250
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:27,840
How horrible!

251
00:15:27,840 --> 00:15:31,020
Sorry. I had to knock out
the old man.

252
00:15:31,020 --> 00:15:32,440
What?!

253
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:35,200
Hold on!
You don't need to tell them that!

254
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:35,900
You saw it.

255
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,540
Yeah, but you had an actual reason–

256
00:15:40,260 --> 00:15:44,660
Why did you guys do this
to our mayor?!

257
00:15:44,660 --> 00:15:46,040
Don't give us your excuses!

258
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:48,880
Who are you?!
Are you with those pirates?!

259
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:51,360
They're really bloodthirsty...

260
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:54,340
If we let it slip that
we're thieves or pirates–

261
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,670
We're pirates!

262
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,340
– Just as we thought!
– Just as we thought!

263
00:16:02,040 --> 00:16:02,840
You idiot!

264
00:16:02,840 --> 00:16:03,700
It's the truth!

265
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:07,240
Pirates! How dare
you ravage our town?!

266
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,060
Kids or not, you're in for it!

267
00:16:10,160 --> 00:16:13,730
What now?
Sounds like they won't hear us out.

268
00:16:15,180 --> 00:16:17,050
Run!

269
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:20,160
There's no escape!

270
00:16:20,160 --> 00:16:23,960
How dare you hurt
our beloved mayor?!

271
00:16:28,340 --> 00:16:31,780
Ugh! Why did you
make things worse?!

272
00:16:31,780 --> 00:16:32,600
This town's good!

273
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,090
Wha...?!

274
00:16:33,090 --> 00:16:37,550
Everyone got so upset
over the old mayor guy!

275
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:45,550
I'd bet giving excuses
would just make things worse!

276
00:16:45,550 --> 00:16:47,230
We're turning here!

277
00:16:47,230 --> 00:16:49,700
H-Hold on!
Give a girl some warning!

278
00:16:49,700 --> 00:16:51,610
They ran into the alley!

279
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:57,700
Chouchou?!

280
00:16:57,700 --> 00:16:59,500
That dog!

281
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:06,420
H-Hey! Move, Chouchou! Hey!

282
00:17:06,420 --> 00:17:08,380
Those guys are bad pirates!

283
00:17:08,380 --> 00:17:09,840
You're barking at the wrong group!

284
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:13,590
Why are you getting in the way?!

285
00:17:13,590 --> 00:17:14,780
Chouchou! Let us past!

286
00:17:18,470 --> 00:17:20,320
Chouchou!

287
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:32,280
Later, dog!

288
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,300
That was scary!

289
00:17:42,300 --> 00:17:44,440
We managed to escape
thanks to Chouchou!

290
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:47,040
Why do we have to put up with this?!

291
00:17:47,040 --> 00:17:50,480
Does it matter now?
We're done here anyway.

292
00:17:50,480 --> 00:17:51,760
Maybe so, but...

293
00:17:51,760 --> 00:17:53,520
Hey, is this your boat?!

294
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:55,080
It's great!

295
00:17:55,080 --> 00:17:57,720
I don't think it's so great.

296
00:17:57,720 --> 00:18:00,000
I stole it from some idiot pirates.

297
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,940
That's a big mouth ya got!

298
00:18:02,970 --> 00:18:05,420
Been waitin' for ya, thief girl!

299
00:18:05,420 --> 00:18:08,100
Never thought you'd run
into us here, didja?!

300
00:18:10,360 --> 00:18:11,480
You know them?

301
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:13,000
Yeah... sort of!

302
00:18:13,000 --> 00:18:16,380
Not sort of! We're bound by fate!

303
00:18:16,380 --> 00:18:20,780
So you had friends, huh?
Guess we'll hafta punish you, too!

304
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:24,460
You'll learn exactly why
you shouldn't steal from others!

305
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:30,200
Hey, you! Wouldja stop
freakin' ignoring me?!

306
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,440
Huh?!

307
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:42,850
Mayor! Are you conscious?!

308
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:46,240
Thank goodness! You're all right!

309
00:18:46,240 --> 00:18:48,310
What in the world happened?!

310
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,800
What in the...?!

311
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:54,360
It was already like this
when we got here!

312
00:18:54,360 --> 00:18:58,300
There were some pirates left,
but they all ran off!

313
00:18:59,030 --> 00:19:01,490
Did you not see anything
that happened?!

314
00:19:01,490 --> 00:19:03,280
Where are those youngsters?!

315
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:03,280
Huh?

316
00:19:03,280 --> 00:19:04,320
"Youngsters"?

317
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:06,620
Do you mean those three kids?

318
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:09,890
So they're alive?!

319
00:19:10,900 --> 00:19:15,090
Those fools! How dare they harm
a senior citizen like me!

320
00:19:17,280 --> 00:19:20,800
We just finished driving
those idiots away!

321
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,140
But it's still not enough!

322
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:25,140
They almost seemed
to be mocking us!

323
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:30,550
They'd never understand how we felt
when they attacked our town!

324
00:19:30,580 --> 00:19:31,320
Yeah! Yeah!

325
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:33,580
There's still time
to go after them and catch–

326
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:35,110
Enough of that!

327
00:19:35,110 --> 00:19:38,030
I'm the only one who's
allowed to complain about them!

328
00:19:38,030 --> 00:19:41,450
I won't let anyone else
talk badly about them!

329
00:19:41,450 --> 00:19:44,530
Wh-What?! Why are you
protecting pirates?!

330
00:19:44,530 --> 00:19:47,860
Damn them... So they plan
to just disappear?!

331
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:49,740
Where did they go?!

332
00:19:49,740 --> 00:19:51,990
They, uh, ran toward the port.

333
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,460
Damn it!

334
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:55,460
Mayor! Mayor!

335
00:19:55,480 --> 00:19:58,760
They think they can do
whatever they please in my town!

336
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:02,720
I have lots to say to you all!

337
00:20:06,140 --> 00:20:08,680
Alright! Let's get going!

338
00:20:08,680 --> 00:20:12,480
Isn't that Buggy's mark
on your sail there?

339
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:15,690
Well, this is his boat.
I'll get rid of it soon.

340
00:20:17,570 --> 00:20:21,340
Hey! Wait! Youngsters!

341
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:22,990
The old mayor guy!

342
00:20:30,840 --> 00:20:33,640
I was ready to die!

343
00:20:33,640 --> 00:20:37,550
I was ready to die filled with despair!

344
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:41,140
Thanks! We're in your debt!

345
00:20:44,240 --> 00:20:47,600
Don't worry about it! Take it easy!

346
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:52,000
Dammit, kiddos. Dammit, kiddos!

347
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:54,810
Dammit, kiddos...

348
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,020
I have no words...

349
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:06,360
What?!

350
00:21:06,360 --> 00:21:08,800
You left one of the treasure bags?!

351
00:21:08,800 --> 00:21:09,260
Yeah.

352
00:21:09,260 --> 00:21:12,280
I'll have you know just one
is worth five million belly!

353
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:15,980
But they need money
to fix their destroyed town, right?

354
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,790
That was my treasure!

355
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:21,260
Do you know how much
I suffered trying to steal it?!

356
00:21:21,260 --> 00:21:23,460
Why did you do that?!

357
00:21:23,460 --> 00:21:25,490
Stop! I can't swim!

358
00:21:25,490 --> 00:21:26,920
That's the whole idea!

359
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:29,220
If you want it,
go back and get it then!

360
00:21:29,220 --> 00:21:31,740
I can't do that! You go get it!

361
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:34,240
No! That's really dangerous!
I could die, you know!

362
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:35,570
Then at least die once!

363
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:39,110
Do that again and I really will
throw you into the ocean!

364
00:21:40,520 --> 00:21:43,460
Well, for better or worse,

365
00:21:43,460 --> 00:21:48,270
looks like a navigator's
joined our journey.
